* LBRHELP - HELP FROM A LIBRARY

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* LBRHELP - HELP FROM A LIBRARY

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:LBRHELP [-[dir:]library] [helpname]

Displays compatible help members stored in an LBR. The optional library
selector chooses a library instead of the configured default.

This is a separate historical help reader; it does not replace public
HELPC or implement the new cross-directory HELPC link syntax. Use LDIR to
inspect a library and LT to read ordinary text members.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
